    const sleepChecklist = {"fr":[{"label":"Faire une pause d’écran avant le coucher","why":"La lumière et les contenus stimulants peuvent garder l’esprit en éveil. Une transition plus calme aide certaines personnes à se préparer au repos.","benefit":"Un endormissement potentiellement plus facile. Si une heure est irréaliste, commence par réduire la luminosité ou éloigner le téléphone."},{"label":"Éviter la caféine en fin de journée","why":"La caféine est stimulante et peut rester active plusieurs heures; la sensibilité varie selon les personnes.","benefit":"Moins de stimulation au moment du coucher et, parfois, moins de difficulté à s’endormir. Essaie une heure limite adaptée à ton rythme."},{"label":"Prendre 10 minutes pour respirer tranquillement","why":"Une respiration lente et confortable ou un moment de relaxation peut aider à relâcher la tension après la journée.","benefit":"Une sensation de calme avant le coucher. Ne force pas le souffle; arrête si tu ressens un inconfort."},{"label":"Garder une heure de réveil assez régulière","why":"Des horaires de réveil proches d’un jour à l’autre donnent un repère stable au rythme veille-sommeil.","benefit":"Le sommeil peut devenir plus prévisible avec le temps. Vise une régularité réaliste, sans culpabiliser si ton emploi du temps change."},{"label":"Rendre la chambre sombre et calme","why":"La lumière et le bruit peuvent interrompre le repos ou maintenir l’attention. Le confort et une température agréable comptent aussi.","benefit":"Moins de distractions pendant la nuit et un environnement plus propice au repos; adapte ces changements à ce qui est possible chez toi."}],"en":[{"label":"Take a screen break before bed","why":"Bright light and stimulating content can keep your mind alert. A calmer transition helps some people prepare for rest.","benefit":"Falling asleep may feel easier. If an hour is not realistic, start by dimming the screen or putting your phone aside."},{"label":"Avoid caffeine late in the day","why":"Caffeine is a stimulant and can remain active for several hours; people vary in how sensitive they are to it.","benefit":"Less stimulation near bedtime and, for some people, less difficulty falling asleep. Choose a cutoff time that fits your routine."},{"label":"Spend 10 minutes breathing calmly","why":"Slow, comfortable breathing or a quiet relaxation practice may ease tension after the day.","benefit":"You may feel calmer before bed. Do not force your breathing; stop if it feels uncomfortable."},{"label":"Keep your wake-up time fairly regular","why":"Waking at similar times gives your sleep-wake rhythm a steadier daily cue.","benefit":"Your sleep schedule may become more predictable over time. Aim for a realistic routine, and allow for changes in your schedule."},{"label":"Make your room dark and quiet","why":"Light and noise can interrupt rest or keep your attention engaged. Comfort and a pleasant temperature matter too.","benefit":"Fewer nighttime distractions and a setting that is more supportive of rest; adapt this to what is practical at home."}],"ar":[{"label":"Take a screen break before bed","why":"Bright light and stimulating content can keep your mind alert. A calmer transition helps some people prepare for rest.","benefit":"Falling asleep may feel easier. If an hour is not realistic, start by dimming the screen or putting your phone aside."},{"label":"Avoid caffeine late in the day","why":"Caffeine is a stimulant and can remain active for several hours; people vary in how sensitive they are to it.","benefit":"Less stimulation near bedtime and, for some people, less difficulty falling asleep. Choose a cutoff time that fits your routine."},{"label":"Spend 10 minutes breathing calmly","why":"Slow, comfortable breathing or a quiet relaxation practice may ease tension after the day.","benefit":"You may feel calmer before bed. Do not force your breathing; stop if it feels uncomfortable."},{"label":"Keep your wake-up time fairly regular","why":"Waking at similar times gives your sleep-wake rhythm a steadier daily cue.","benefit":"Your sleep schedule may become more predictable over time. Aim for a realistic routine, and allow for changes in your schedule."},{"label":"Make your room dark and quiet","why":"Light and noise can interrupt rest or keep your attention engaged. Comfort and a pleasant temperature matter too.","benefit":"Fewer nighttime distractions and a setting that is more supportive of rest; adapt this to what is practical at home."}],"darija":[{"label":"Take a screen break before bed","why":"Bright light and stimulating content can keep your mind alert. A calmer transition helps some people prepare for rest.","benefit":"Falling asleep may feel easier. If an hour is not realistic, start by dimming the screen or putting your phone aside."},{"label":"Avoid caffeine late in the day","why":"Caffeine is a stimulant and can remain active for several hours; people vary in how sensitive they are to it.","benefit":"Less stimulation near bedtime and, for some people, less difficulty falling asleep. Choose a cutoff time that fits your routine."},{"label":"Spend 10 minutes breathing calmly","why":"Slow, comfortable breathing or a quiet relaxation practice may ease tension after the day.","benefit":"You may feel calmer before bed. Do not force your breathing; stop if it feels uncomfortable."},{"label":"Keep your wake-up time fairly regular","why":"Waking at similar times gives your sleep-wake rhythm a steadier daily cue.","benefit":"Your sleep schedule may become more predictable over time. Aim for a realistic routine, and allow for changes in your schedule."},{"label":"Make your room dark and quiet","why":"Light and noise can interrupt rest or keep your attention engaged. Comfort and a pleasant temperature matter too.","benefit":"Fewer nighttime distractions and a setting that is more supportive of rest; adapt this to what is practical at home."}]};

